[0.574,"m","Deploy (--mode assisted): ov prints the commands and runs nothing"]
[0.574,"o","$ "]
[0.575,"o","ov stack deploy ov-e2ep-s130649 --cloud azure --azure-location \"$AZURE_LOCATION\" --edition pro --openvidu-pro-license \"$OPENVIDU_PRO_LICENSE\" --certificate-type selfsigned --mode assisted\r\n"]
[3.835,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[4.44,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nRun these commands yourself in your Azure subscription (location northeurope); ov runs none of them.\r\nOnce they have finished, run this same command again: ov finds the machines and ends the deploy.\r\n\r\n  # SSH access: the key pair for this stack, its public half handed to the template.\r\n  #   .openvidu/azure/ov-e2ep-s130649-key.pub\r\n  # The template, rendered from the one embedded in this CLI for the single node topology,\r\n  # written out for you to read (az compiles the Bicep itself):\r\n  #   .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-pro-singlenode.bicep\r\n  # Its secure parameters (the license), in a 0600 parameters file rather than on\r\n  # the command line, which any user of this machine would see:\r\n  #   .openvidu/azure/secure-parameters.json\r\n  az group create --name ov-e2ep-s130649-rg --location northeurope --tags created-by=openvidu-cli --only-show-errors -o none\r\n  # Create the machines. deployedBy=instance: master-1 installs OpenVidu with the\r\n  # OpenVidu CLI and the other nodes join it. The command returns when Azure is done (about 4 minutes).\r\n  az deployment group create --resource-group ov-e2ep-s130649-rg --name ov-e2ep-s130649 --template-file .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-pro-singlenode.bicep --only-show-errors --query properties.provisioningState -o tsv --parameters certificateType=selfsigned deployedBy=instance registryStorage=false stackName=ov-e2ep-s130649 'publicIpAddressObject={\"newOrExistingOrNone\":\"new\",\"name\":\"ov-e2ep-s130649-pip\"}' adminSshKey=\"{\\\"sshPublicKey\\\":\\\"$(cat .openvidu/azure/ov-e2ep-s130649-key.pub)\\\"}\" --parameters @.openvidu/azure/secure-parameters.json\r\n\r\n  # What the stack published: URL, credentials and the stack's access, as secrets in the Key Vault the deployment outputs (KUBECONFIG\r\n  # appears once OpenVidu is up: until then this read fails, and ov waits for it).\r\n  az deployment group show --resource-group ov-e2ep-s130649-rg --name ov-e2ep-s130649 --query properties.outputs -o json\r\n  KV=\"$(az deployment group show --resource-group ov-e2ep-s130649-rg --name ov-e2ep-s130649 --query properties.outputs.sharedInfoKeyVault.value -o tsv)\"\r\n  az keyvault secret show --vault-name $KV --name KUBECONFIG --query value -o tsv\r\n\r\nNothing above has been run. Once these commands have finished, run this same command again:\r\n\r\n  ov stack deploy ov-e2ep-s130649 --cloud azure --mode assisted\r\n\r\nIt finds the machines, waits for OpenVidu to come up and registers this directory as the\r\nstack. It creates nothing in your account.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
